## Final Judgement
**Summary of Key Insights**  
The evidence confirms that a fatal shooting occurred in Denver on October 10, 2020, during dueling protests. However, the shooter was identified by law enforcement as a private security guard hired by a Denver TV station—not a BLM or antifa activist. Police explicitly stated the guard had "no affiliation with Antifa," and multiple sources corroborate this. The victim was affiliated with a right-wing "Patriot Rally," but the shooting was deemed unrelated to political motive.

**Lacking Information**  
No further information is needed; the evidence is clear and consistent in refuting the claim's assertion about the shooter's identity.

**Conclusion**  
The claim states a "BLM or antifa activist" shot and killed a patriot in Denver on October 10, 2020. The recorded evidence from multiple authoritative sources—including law enforcement statements and news reports—directly contradicts this by identifying the shooter as a private security guard with no affiliation to BLM or antifa. Therefore, the claim is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
While a fatal shooting did occur near dueling protests in Denver on October 10, 2020, law enforcement identified the shooter as Matthew Dolloff, a [private security guard](https://gephardtdaily.com/top-stories/man-fatally-shot-during-clash-between-opposing-protest-groups-in-denver/) hired by Denver TV station [9News](https://coloradonewsline.com/2020/10/10/man-shot-and-killed-after-patriot-muster-in-downtown-denver/), not a BLM or antifa activist. Denver Police explicitly stated the suspect had "[no affiliation with Antifa](https://www.cbsnews.com/news/one-dead-in-shooting-at-dueling-denver-protests/)," and investigators determined the shooting was not politically motivated, arising instead from a confrontation involving mace in which self-defense was claimed ([Denver7](https://www.denver7.com/news/local-news/1-shot-during-protests-in-denver-2-suspects-in-custody)). The victim, Lee Keltner, was affiliated with a right-wing "Patriot Rally" ([Gephardt Daily](https://gephardtdaily.com/top-stories/man-fatally-shot-during-clash-between-opposing-protest-groups-in-denver/)), but multiple independent sources consistently contradicted the claim's characterization of the shooter, leading to a verdict of **refuted**.